Certainly not the driver.  It could probably be fixed by altering 
pci_drvmessage() in pci_compat.c..  That's probably not the right way, 
however.

 > gpr:       1A (   R26) FFFFFC000036CA64
 > 
 > is that supposed to be meaningful? :-)
