(gdb) l *0xFFFFFC000036CA64 

I think there's a gdb floating around someplace..
If you don't have one, grab ftp://ftp.cs.duke.edu/pub/gallatin/gdb.gz 
That's a hacked up cross-pollenated NetBSD gdb that will do live
kernel debugging as well if you tell it to 'target kcore /dev/mem'

